IMPORT `ab79-nouns`
IMPORT `ab79-cross-references`

-- Row il-79. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the cited ones, and the values pinned to what the quotation lines print. They pass.
-- C1: SH 233 section 19 prints a lettered subsection (b), the letter the citing words of section 38 cite; the cited number 19 is the number SH 233 prints.
-- C2: the section 8 that SH 400 section 5 prints has lettered subsections (b) and (d), the letters the citing words cite; the cited number 8 is the number it prints.
-- C3: SH 1123 prints the bracketed references beside sections 41, 96 and 52, where the test finds them.
-- C4: the tables print what they print: under the heading for the previous section 19 with 41 beside it (SH 1123, sub-heading for the 1957 Law), 8 with 12 (NV 19), 12 with 96 (SH 1123, sub-heading for the 1971 new version); the two last chain; each of the three comparisons the red module asks, negated, passes here.
-- C5: SH 1110 section 3 names four sections of the 1957 Law, and 19 is not among them.
-- C6: the instruments are typed Printed and dated by their footers; the New Version prints no issue date.
-- C7 (I2): SH 2760 section 1 names section 1 of the Law; SH 2760 section 2 names a section of another law; the string of the defined term occurs in section 38 as printed in 1968; the 1984 section 52(b) and 41(b) contain the words of a court of each kind.
-- C8: the consolidation's lines, which are CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
-- C9: sections 1 and 25 of the Interpretation Law are typed as printed.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in ab79-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

